WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.536
In this video, you'll tour the Tracking tab — a second set of FedEx keys used only for tracking, plus its webhook setup.

00:00:07.986 --> 00:00:12.138
You'll find it under FedEx Shipping, then Settings, in your store's admin.

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:20.196
FedEx projects are usually split by API family, so tracking gets its own key and secret — and its own tab here.

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:28.230
There's no fallback to your main keys — leave this tab empty and rates and labels work, but tracking quietly dies.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:37.872
Below the credentials sits the Tracking Webhooks section — FedEx pushes updates there automatically as a parcel moves. AIV is FedEx's name for it.

00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:44.538
It has two parts: your store's webhook address with a Copy button, and a Webhook Shared Secret field.

00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:50.484
Copy the address and paste it into your FedEx project — the plugin can't do that step for you.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:58.974
Set the same shared secret in FedEx and here, then Save Changes. Until the two match exactly, updates are turned away.

00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:06.264
An empty secret blocks every update on purpose — it stops anyone sending your store fake tracking events.

00:01:06.714 --> 00:01:13.386
The tracking form works without the webhook — it asks FedEx directly. Next, continue to the Account tab.

